\date{2024-09-12}
\author{fredrikbakke}
\taxon{Definition}
\import{common}
\title{Transposing adjunctions}

\p{Given a pair of maps of simplicial types #{L \colon X \to Y} and #{R \colon Y \to X}, we say #{L} is a \concept{left adjoint} to #{R}, and that #{R} is a \concept{right adjoint} to #{L} if we have a binary family of [equivalences](hott-000U)
##{\pi-type{x:X,y : Y}{(\hom_Y(L(x),y) \simeq \hom_X(x,R(y)))}.}}
